{"type":"text","timestamp":1785550049129,"sessionID":"ses_04501cd40ffewOC0br6SKhywMQ","part":{"id":"prt_fbb136b81001adGVm68It5DHkj","messageID":"msg_fbb1363ab001kE7jO25WBkmNm2","sessionID":"ses_04501cd40ffewOC0br6SKhywMQ","type":"text","text":"Done. The Brazilian Soccer MCP server is implemented, builds, and **168 tests pass** (23 BDD scenarios + unit/functional/MCP-integration tests).\n\n## What was built\n\n**Package `brazilian_soccer_mcp/`**\n- `normalization.py` — team-name normalization (state suffixes `\"Palmeiras-SP\"`, full names `\"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"`, accents `\"Grêmio\"`/`\"Gremio\"`, club tokens `\"Fortaleza FC\"`), alias table with state disambiguation (`América-MG` ≠ `América-RN`), multi-format date parsing (ISO, ISO+time, `DD/MM/YYYY`), and a fuzzy team registry.\n- `data_loader.py` — loads all 6 CSVs into one unified match table + FIFA player table. Handles cross-file fixture deduplication (same-day, same-fixture, adjacent-day passes), corrects the extended file's derived seasons (COVID-delayed 2020 season, cup cross-referencing), and drops bogus mislabeled rows.\n- `queries.py` — query engine for all 5 spec capabilities: match search, head-to-head, team records (home/away splits), standings (3/1/0 pts, champion, relegation), player search/profile/rosters, biggest wins, competition stats, season comparison, top scorers.\n- `server.py` — FastMCP server with **16 MCP tools** returning spec-formatted text; runs over stdio (`python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp`) or HTTP.\n\n**Tests** — `tests/`: normalization unit tests, loader tests (raw row counts vs spec, schema, dedupe), 60+ functional query tests, 5 Gherkin feature files with 23 pytest-bdd scenarios, and MCP integration tests including a real stdio subprocess handshake. Performance assertions (lookups <2s, aggregates <5s) included.\n\n**Data quality verified**: computed standings reproduce real history exactly for all 11 fully-covered seasons — e.g. 2019 Flamengo 90 pts (28W 6D 4L), 2018 Palmeiras 80, 2020 Flamengo 71, 2021 Atlético-MG 84, 2022 Palmeiras 81 — each with exactly 380 matches.\n\n**Packaging**: `pyproject.toml` (wheel build verified), `requirements.txt`, `pytest.ini`, README usage section documenting architecture, tools, and known source-data limitations (2023 partial coverage, FIFA 19 club licensing gaps).","time":{"start":1785550039937,"end":1785550049126}}}
